1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,420
Landing near the Moon's south pole?

2
00:00:02,420 --> 00:00:06,100
You need sunlight for power,
and Earth in view for radio.

3
00:00:06,100 --> 00:00:08,480
This is one site's sky for a year.

4
00:00:08,480 --> 00:00:11,240
Grey is the real NASA terrain skyline.

5
00:00:11,240 --> 00:00:14,700
When the Sun sinks behind it,
the lander goes dark.

6
00:00:14,700 --> 00:00:17,100
Each card scores a site:
time in sunlight,

7
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,600
time Earth is in view,
and the longest dark spell.

8
00:00:20,600 --> 00:00:23,240
The heatmap shows the best days to land.

9
00:00:23,240 --> 00:00:26,000
Click one, and every number updates.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,490
Too close to call?

11
00:00:27,490 --> 00:00:29,500
It tells you, honestly.
